<p>Hello!</p>

<p>It's been a few months since I've finished <a href="/read"><i>IA IA IA</i></a>. I've been very appreciative of the response to it, especially everyone's reactions to the last chapter. It was a lot of fun seeing what everyone took from it.</p>

<p>I said I'd take a break when I finished <i>IA IA IA</i>. As a matter of fact, to a certain extent, I was forced to take a break. After I finished the comic over New Years', I spent a few months getting the print version ready. In April, I put out the print version, and again I was very thankful for the reception it got. Unfortunately, one month later, I was laid off from my job.<p>

<p>The last few months have been very busy for me as a result. I was already in the process of buying a house when I lost my job, and I decided I still wanted to go through with the purchase (time will tell whether or not that was a good decision). The rest of my time goes to job hunting, household chores, or the few hobbies I can continue to indulge in without spending a lot of money. Unfortunately, no jobs have materialized in the intervening time, but I'm still trying hard to find something.</p>

<p>As always, if you want to throw some money my way in the meantime, you can <a href="/store">buy a copy of <i>IA IA IA</i></a>, or you can <a href="https://www.patreon.com/c/IAIAIAWORLD">support me on Patreon</a>.</p>

<p>That's the sad stuff out of the way. In other news, I've started a new comic! It's called NIB, and I'm still sort of working on the pitch. It's a bit like if Dick Tracy and Prince Valiant had a baby, and that baby was a funny animals comic, using the material history of newspaper comics as a spine (although that might be promising too much). It's going to update daily (I hope), just like a newspaper comic would. I hope you enjoy it!</p>

<p><a href="/nib">You can read NIB here.</a></p>